WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.257
A view can reduce accidental exposure by publishing only the columns required for an analytical task.

00:00:06.257 --> 00:00:12.757
For example, an analytics interface may expose an age band and city instead of direct contact fields.

00:00:12.757 --> 00:00:18.117
But hiding columns in a view definition is not the same as granting or denying access.

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:22.882
Actual authorization depends on PostgreSQL privileges and, where appropriate,

00:00:22.882 --> 00:00:25.512
row-level security or other controls.

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:30.292
A standard view stores a query definition, not a separate copy of the rows.

00:00:30.292 --> 00:00:36.492
Treat the selected columns, names, types, and grain as a contract with downstream users.

00:00:36.492 --> 00:00:42.566
Changing that contract can break dashboards or applications even if the underlying query still runs.
